1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,700
SHIRLEY: Hello?

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:08,680
TOM: Oh hello. I was hoping to speak to Jack Fitzgerald about renting a cottage.

3
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:12,700
SHIRLEY: I'm his wife, Shirley, and we own the cottages together

4
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:14,160
so I'm sure I can help you.

5
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:16,630
TOM: Great. My name's Tom.

6
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:20,820
Some friends of ours rented Granary Cottage from you last year

7
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,250
and they thought it was great.

8
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:26,040
So my wife and I are hoping to come in May for a week.

9
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:28,600
SHIRLEY: What date did you have in mind?

10
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:32,250
TOM: The week beginning the 14th, if possible.

11
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:38,510
SHIRLEY: I'll just check... I'm sorry, Tom, it's already booked that week.

12
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:43,480
It's free the week beginning the 28th, though, for seven nights.

13
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:47,310
In fact, that's the only time you could have it in May.

14
00:00:47,310 --> 00:00:51,150
TOM: Oh. Well, we could manage that, I think.

15
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:54,460
We'd just need to change a couple of things.

16
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:56,540
How much would it cost?

17
00:00:56,540 --> 00:01:03,040
SHIRLEY: That's the beginning of high season, so it'd be £550 for the week.

18
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:07,690
TOM: Ah. That's a bit more than we wanted to pay, I'm afraid.

19
00:01:07,690 --> 00:01:12,130
We've budgeted up to £500 for accommodation.

20
00:01:12,130 --> 00:01:17,486
SHIRLEY: Well, we've just finished converting another building into a cottage,

21
00:01:17,486 --> 00:01:19,920
which we're calling Chervil Cottage.

22
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:22,120
TOM: Sorry? What was that again?

23
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:30,500
SHIRLEY: Chervil. C-H-E-R-V for Victor I-L.

24
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,820
TOM: Oh, that's a herb, isn't it?

25
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:36,610
SHIRLEY: That's right. It grows fairly wild around here.

26
00:01:36,610 --> 00:01:41,160
You could have that for the week you want for £480.

27
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:45,460
TOM: OK. So could you tell me something about it, please?

28
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:50,000
SHIRLEY: Of course. The building was built as a garage.

29
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,080
It's a little smaller than Granary Cottage.

30
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,760
TOM: So that must sleep two people, as well?

31
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,550
SHIRLEY: That's right. There's a double bedroom.

32
00:01:58,550 --> 00:01:59,800
TOM: Does it have a garden?

33
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:04,520
SHIRLEY: Yes, you get to it from the living room through French doors

34
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:06,900
and we provide two deckchairs.

35
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:10,400
We hope to build a patio in the near future

36
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:13,520
but I wouldn't like to guarantee it'll be finished by May.

37
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,330
TOM: OK.

38
00:02:14,330 --> 00:02:20,297
SHIRLEY: The front door opens onto the old farmyard,

39
00:02:20,297 --> 00:02:29,580
and parking isn't a problem - there's plenty of room at the front for that.

40
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:32,860
TOM: What about facilities in the cottage?

41
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:37,160
It has standard things like a cooker and fridge, I presume.

42
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:44,020
SHIRLEY: In the kitchen area there's a fridge-freezer and we've just put in an electric cooker.

43
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:46,290
Is there a washing machine?

44
00:02:46,290 --> 00:02:52,230
TOM: Yes. There's also a TV in the living room, which plays DVDs too.

45
00:02:52,230 --> 00:02:58,260
The bathroom is too small for a bath, so there's a shower instead.

46
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:01,780
I think a lot of people prefer that nowadays, anyway.

47
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:04,500
TOM: It's more environmentally friendly, isn't it?

48
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,600
Unless you spend half the day in it!

49
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,250
SHIRLEY: Exactly.

50
00:03:07,250 --> 00:03:12,170
TOM: What about heating? It sometimes gets quite cool at that time of year.

51
00:03:12,170 --> 00:03:17,230
SHIRLEY: There's central heating, and if you want to light a fire, there's a stove.

52
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:20,520
We can provide all the wood you need for it.

53
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:23,380
It smells so much nicer than coal

54
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:27,740
and it makes the room very cosy - we've got one in our own house.

55
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,480
TOM: That sounds very pleasant.

56
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:33,060
Perhaps we should come in the winter, to make the most of it!

57
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:37,430
SHIRLEY: Yes, we find we don't want to go out when we've got the fire burning.

58
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:42,260
There are some attractive views from the cottage, which I haven't mentioned.

59
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:45,060
There's a famous stone bridge

60
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:49,840
it's one of the oldest in the region, and you can see it from the living room.

61
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:51,700
It isn't far away.

62
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:54,536
The bedroom window looks in the opposite direction,

63
00:03:54,536 --> 00:03:59,500
and has a lovely view of the hills and the monument at the top.

64
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:02,360
TOM: Well, that all sounds perfect.

65
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:05,730
I'd like to book it, please. Would you want a deposit?

66
00:04:05,730 --> 00:04:10,300
SHIRLEY: Yes, we ask for thirty percent to secure your booking

67
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:14,460
so that'll be, um, £144.

68
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:17,270
TOM: And when would you like the rest of the money?

69
00:04:17,270 --> 00:04:22,110
SHIRLEY: You're coming in May, so the last day of March, please.

70
00:04:22,110 --> 00:04:23,160
TOM: Fine.

71
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:28,000
SHIRLEY: Excellent. Could I just take your details...
